    "id": "perflab_cache_miss_severe",
    "cause_family": "cache_miss",
    "profile": "spring-boot",
    "setup": "Set perflab.cache.enabled=false in application.properties. Drive /api/catalog at 50 users. The catalog endpoint reads data that does not change between requests; disabling the cache makes every read a DB roundtrip. Pool fields show moderate pressure (connections are held longer than they need to be); the distinguishing fact is that the same query runs on every request without variation.\n",
    "task_classes": [
      "A"
    ],
    "trap_properties": [],
    "bottleneck_config": {
      "perflab.cache.enabled": false,
      "endpoint": "/api/catalog"
    },
    "severity": "severe",
    "validated_at": "",
    "scenario_tag": "catalog",
    "providers": [
      "actuator"
    ],
    "notes": "The cache_miss diagnosis requires the agent to identify that pool pressure is SECONDARY (more connections are held longer because each read is slower) while cache_miss is PRIMARY. An agent that raises the pool size on this fixture is taking the wrong fork: it addresses the secondary symptom and leaves the primary cause untouched, and the pool fix will improve numbers more than pool_exhaustion would justify -- because the improvement comes from the DB being slightly less busy, not from more connections being available.\n"
  },
